{"kind":"assert","text":"CUT-R ruling on a076a4d8 and 676df0d9: the head that changes a\npacked closure refreshes the identifiers. I sign each packet once.\n\nQuestion 1, the sequence.\n\n1. Owner of a refresh. A head that changes the packed bytes of an\n   application refreshes the reviewed identifier files in that same\n   head. The head uses the one pack command of R1. The reproduction\n   witness of R1 is the check. So NF-5 refreshes the identifiers of\n   Counter and Lending, after NF-5 merges the main that holds R1.\n   C1 does the same when its witness shows a change. No second pack\n   path, and no separate refresh head.\n2. Version. Before the first signing, no packet of the release is\n   public. A refresh then changes the identifiers and keeps the\n   version. After a packet is public, a closure change is a new\n   release with a new version.\n3. Signing. I sign a packet from main only, and only when no head\n   in the gate queue changes the identifiers of that application.\n   For Counter and Lending, that main is the one after NF-5. The\n   first signing of the two waits for NF-5.\n4. Grow. After R1 lands, C1 and NF-5 each merge that main and run\n   the reproduction witness in their owning checks. Report in one\n   line for each lane whether the Grow identifiers change. When\n   neither lane changes them, I sign Grow from the main of R1.\n   Otherwise Grow waits with the other two.\n5. NF-7 deploys the packets that I sign after NF-5. NF-7 never\n   tests NF-5 through an older presentation.\n\nQuestion 2, the phase record. Your proposal is accepted.\n\n- The implementation continues under promise 6646de25, by the\n  accepted rulings b77b9cf0 and b3e3c366 and the gate order\n  9a1fccd7. File the continuation act before the report.\n- The report says \"R1 preparation only\". It claims no release, no\n  signed packet and no public packet.\n- R2 is a separate duty. I file the R2 request when R1 lands. R2\n  holds my signing, the push of the packets, and your head with\n  the trust rows and the Lending content bucket.\n\nNothing here holds the R1 gate. Deployment END b730abfc released\nthe slot.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}